# Binary game data and assets must NEVER get line-ending conversion. Without
# this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true injects \r bytes into these
# binary files, corrupting them - e.g. a .map then fails ZMap::Read and the
# engine falls back to its featureless random map. (macOS/Linux were unaffected,
# so this was a Windows-only "garbage map" bug.)
*.map       binary
*.bmp       binary
*.png       binary
*.ico       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.wav       binary
*.ogg       binary
*.mid       binary
*.tileinfo  binary
*.xcf       binary
*.icescene  binary
*.rar       binary
*.zip       binary
*.db        binary
*.o         binary
*.LST       binary
*.MID       binary

# Source and text data: normalize to LF in the repo. map_list.txt is parsed
# with clean_newline(), which strips \r, so its endings don't matter at runtime.
*.cpp  text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
